   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( f(x) = 3 x^{2} + 3 \\). The region R shown is bounded by the graph of f, the line \\( y = 3 \\), and the vertical line \\( x = 5 \\). Find the exact volume of the solid generated when R is revolved about the line \\( y = 3 \\).",
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Multiply",
         5625,
         "Pi"
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Each slice perpendicular to the x-axis is a disc whose radius is the distance from the curve to the axis, \\( r = f(x) - 3 = 3 x^{2} \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99058",
         "rule_named": "disc radius"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The volume is \\( \\pi\\int_{0}^{5} \\left(3 x^{2}\\right)^{2}\\,dx \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99001",
         "rule_named": "disc method"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Since \\( \\int_{0}^{5} 9 x^{4}\\,dx = 5625 \\), the volume is \\( 5625 \\pi \\).",
